# Zurgo's protection is only for Warrior tokens during its controller's end step (CR 604.1, 613.1f, 701.21a). Bot1's Ashnod's
# Altar sacrifices a creature for {C}{C}: in the declare blockers step, a mobilized Warrior token is sacrificed with no trouble;
# in the end step, once mobilize's sacrifice has resolved to nothing, the other token can't be (the refusal) but Zurgo itself, a Warrior card and not a token, can be, and does.
# The sacrificed Warrior deals no combat damage: Zurgo 2 + the one Warrior left 1 = 3, so Bot2 is at 17.

[Bot1 Deck]
